        "title": {
          "en": "At the zoo"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "At the zoo Teja watched a deer nibbling grass and a lion resting near some meat. A crow nearby pecked at both fruit and a small insect.\n\"Why do they eat different things?\" he asked the guide."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "herbivore",
          "carnivore",
          "omnivore",
          "teeth"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "Animals that eat only plants are called herbivores, such as cows, deer and elephants. Animals that eat only other animals are called carnivores, such as lions, tigers and eagles.\nAnimals that eat both plants and animals are called omnivores, such as crows, bears and humans.\nTheir bodies suit their food. Herbivores have flat teeth to grind plants. Carnivores have sharp pointed teeth to tear meat."
        }
      },
